<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Milli - Baby Tracker Support</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Support, privacy, and account deletion information for Milli - Baby Tracker."
    />
    <style>
      :root {
        --bg: #ffffff;
        --text: #17202a;
        --muted: #5f6b7a;
        --panel: #f7f8fa;
        --border: #dfe5ec;
        --brand: #6f4fc6;
        --brand-dark: #4d358c;
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.6;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
      }

      header {
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        background: var(--panel);
      }

      main,
      .container {
        width: min(100% - 32px, 860px);
        margin: 0 auto;
      }

      header .container {
        padding: 28px 0;
      }

      main {
        padding: 28px 0 48px;
      }

      h1 {
        margin: 0 0 8px;
        font-size: 32px;
        line-height: 1.2;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      h2 {
        margin: 34px 0 10px;
        font-size: 22px;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      h3 {
        margin: 20px 0 8px;
        font-size: 18px;
      }

      p {
        margin: 10px 0;
      }

      ul,
      ol {
        margin: 10px 0 10px 22px;
        padding: 0;
      }

      li {
        margin: 6px 0;
      }

      a {
        color: var(--brand-dark);
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      nav {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 12px;
        margin-top: 16px;
      }

      nav a {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 8px 10px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 6px;
        background: #ffffff;
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      .subtitle {
        margin: 0;
        color: var(--muted);
      }

      .box {
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-left: 4px solid var(--brand);
        border-radius: 6px;
        background: var(--panel);
        padding: 16px;
        margin: 14px 0;
      }

      .contact {
        border-color: var(--brand);
        background: #fbf9ff;
      }

      .small {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 14px;
      }

      footer {
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
        background: var(--panel);
      }

      footer .container {
        padding: 18px 0;
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header>
      <div class="container">
        <h1>Milli - Baby Tracker Support</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">
          Support, privacy, and account deletion information for Milli - Baby Tracker.
        </p>
        <nav aria-label="Page sections">
          <a href="#support">Support</a>
          <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
          <a href="#delete-account">Delete Account</a>
          <a href="#privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
          <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section id="support">
        <h2>Support</h2>
        <p>
          Milli - Baby Tracker helps parents and caregivers track feeding, sleep, diapers,
          medicine, symptoms, growth, reminders, and shared family care activity.
        </p>
        <div class="box contact">
          <p>
            For help with the app, account access, family sharing, privacy requests, or data
            deletion, email:
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>
              <a href="mailto:mobileapplicationplaysystems@gmail.com">
                mobileapplicationplaysystems@gmail.com
              </a>
            </strong>
          </p>
          <p class="small">We aim to respond to support and privacy requests within 30 days.</p>
        </div>
        <p><strong>App name:</strong> Milli - Baby Tracker</p>
        <p><strong>Bundle ID:</strong> com.milli.babymonitor</p>
      </section>

      <section id="faq">
        <h2>FAQ</h2>

        <h3>How do I get help?</h3>
        <p>
          Email us with the email address connected to your Milli account and a short description
          of the issue.
        </p>

        <h3>Can I delete individual tracking records?</h3>
        <p>
          Yes. Open the History screen in the app and delete individual tracking entries before
          deleting your account if you want those entries removed.
        </p>

        <h3>Can I turn off notifications?</h3>
        <p>
          Yes. You can disable reminders and notifications in Milli settings or through your
          device notification settings.
        </p>

        <h3>Is baby data used for analytics or ads?</h3>
        <p>
          No. Baby names, health records, and care log contents are not shared with Firebase
          Analytics or Google AdMob.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="delete-account">
        <h2>Delete Your Account</h2>
        <p>
          This section explains how to request deletion of your account and associated data from
          Milli - Baby Tracker.
        </p>

        <div class="box">
          <ol>
            <li>Open the Milli - Baby Tracker app.</li>
            <li>Go to <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Delete Account</strong>.</li>
            <li>Confirm the deletion request.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <p>
          If you cannot access the app, you may request account deletion by emailing
          <a href="mailto:mobileapplicationplaysystems@gmail.com">
            mobileapplicationplaysystems@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>What Data Is Deleted</h3>
        <p>When your account is deleted, the following data will be permanently removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your account email and authentication data</li>
          <li>Baby tracking logs, including feeding, sleep, diaper, medicine, growth, and symptoms</li>
          <li>Family collaboration data and roles, where applicable</li>
          <li>Push notification tokens</li>
          <li>Stored preferences linked to your account</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Data Retention</h3>
        <p>
          Account deletion is processed immediately after confirmation. Some limited technical
          logs may be retained for up to 30 days for security, fraud prevention, backup, and legal
          compliance purposes.
        </p>
        <p>
          If other members remain in your family group, shared tracking entries may remain as
          family records unless you delete those entries before deleting your account or contact us
          for help.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="privacy">
        <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p class="small"><strong>Effective Date:</strong> April 5, 2026</p>
        <p>
          Milli - Baby Tracker ("Milli," "we," "our," or "us") helps families track baby care
          activities. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, how
          it is shared, and your choices.
        </p>

        <h3>Information We Collect</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Account information:</strong> email address and authentication data managed
            through Supabase Authentication.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Family and collaboration data:</strong> family name, family member email,
            role, title, invite codes, and join requests.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Baby care tracking data:</strong> logs created by parents or caregivers, such
            as feeding, diaper, sleep, shower, vitamin, growth, medicine, and symptom or activity
            entries.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Optional baby profile data:</strong> baby name, age, gender, and date of birth,
            if you choose to enter it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Notification data:</strong> device push token, platform, and reminder settings.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Local app data:</strong> cached logs and settings stored on your device to
            support offline use and faster performance.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Analytics data:</strong> Firebase Analytics may collect device and app usage
            data about the parent's or caregiver's session, such as app instance identifier, device
            model, OS version, app version, approximate country or region, session duration, and
            feature usage.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Advertising data:</strong> Google AdMob may collect device identifiers, IP
            address, and general usage signals for ad serving and measurement.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>How We Use Information</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>To provide tracking, history, insights, reminders, and family sharing features</li>
          <li>To sync data across devices and family members in the same family group</li>
          <li>To send reminders and family activity notifications</li>
          <li>To support account and family management</li>
          <li>To improve the app using analytics that does not include baby data</li>
          <li>To display ads through Google AdMob</li>
          <li>To maintain app reliability and security</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>How Information Is Shared</h3>
        <p>We do not sell personal information.</p>
        <p>We may share data only as needed with:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your family group members, based on family membership and permissions in the app</li>
          <li>
            Supabase, for authentication and database services:
            <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              https://supabase.com/privacy</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            Expo Push Notification Service, for notification delivery:
            <a href="https://expo.dev/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              https://expo.dev/privacy</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            Google Firebase Analytics and Google AdMob:
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>
          </li>
          <li>Legal or compliance recipients where required by law or to protect rights and safety</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Baby Data</h3>
        <p>
          Milli is used by parents and caregivers. Babies and children do not create accounts or
          interact with the app. Baby health and care data is sensitive. It is shared only with
          family members you invite and is never shared with Firebase Analytics or Google AdMob.
        </p>

        <h3>Analytics And Advertising</h3>
        <p>
          Firebase Analytics receives device and usage data about the parent's or caregiver's app
          session. It does not receive baby names, health records, care log contents, temperature
          readings, medication details, or tracking field contents.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google AdMob may collect device advertising identifiers, IP address, general location,
          and app usage signals to serve and measure ads. We do not pass baby care tracking data
          or family information to AdMob.
        </p>

        <h3>Your Choices And Rights</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Update your account email and password</li>
          <li>Edit or delete individual tracking entries</li>
          <li>Delete your account and associated data from within the app</li>
          <li>Leave a family group</li>
          <li>Disable notifications in app settings or device settings</li>
          <li>Opt out of personalized ads through your device settings</li>
          <li>Contact us to request access, deletion, correction, or export of your data</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Security</h3>
        <p>
          We use reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect your information,
          including encrypted data transmission, row-level access controls, and restricted access
          to production systems. No method of storage or transmission is 100% secure.
        </p>

        <h3>Changes To This Policy</h3>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The effective date above shows the
          latest version date. For material changes, we will notify users where reasonably
          possible.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <div class="box contact">
          <p><strong>Milli - Baby Tracker</strong></p>
          <p>
            Email:
            <strong>
              <a href="mailto:mobileapplicationplaysystems@gmail.com">
                mobileapplicationplaysystems@gmail.com
              </a>
            </strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            Contact us for app support, account deletion, privacy questions, data access, data
            export, or other data rights requests.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

